## Diagnosis (this checkout — do not re-litigate)

There is **no selected mode**. Desktop click immediately mounts an `<input>`. Navigation is a DOM hack, not a grid state machine. Plan cells are not in the nav graph.

### Why column movement is missing (this is the user-reported gap)

**There is no horizontal nav at all.** Confirm in this checkout before writing code:

1. `EditablePerformanceCell.tsx` `onKeyDown` handles **only** `Enter`, `ArrowDown`, `ArrowUp`, `Escape`. There is **no** `Tab`, `Shift+Tab`, `ArrowLeft`, or `ArrowRight`. Column movement cannot happen.
2. Vertical nav (Enter / ArrowUp / ArrowDown) uses `document.getElementById(\`cell-${fieldKey}-${rowIndex ± 1}\`).click()`. That id is **column-scoped** (`fieldKey` is the same cell type). It never steps kg→reps→rpe, never crosses PLAN→LOG, and `.click()` **re-enters edit** on the destination.
3. `PrescriptionEditor.tsx` never passes `rowIndex` (prop is optional). PLAN kg/reps/rpe therefore have **no** `id="cell-…"`. Enter on a PLAN cell commits and stays. PLAN is off the nav graph.
4. PLAN `fieldKey`s (`"rx-weight"`, `"reps"`, `"targetValue"`) are **not** lift- or row-unique. Even if `rowIndex` were added tomorrow, `getElementById` would collide across lifts/rows.
5. LOG cells in `ExerciseCard.tsx:361-397` **do** pass `rowIndex={i}` and lift-scoped `fieldKey`s. Only LOG vertical “next same column” works, and only while editing.
6. Chrome between columns (`×`, `@`, plan→log `ArrowRight` button, RPE/% toggle) are DOM siblings. Any “move to next focusable” that follows the DOM will land on the copy button or the unit toggle. The 6-col matrix must skip them **by address**, not by `nextElementSibling`.

Until PLAN cells get `rowIndex` + lift identity **and** a shared 6-col neighbor function, Tab / Left / Right / Enter-to-next-row will keep failing.

