## Two modes (steal this split; do not add a library)

Open-source grids (Handsontable keyboard contexts, Luckysheet/Univer editor overlay, WAI-ARIA APG **grid** + roving tabindex) all split:

| Mode | Look | Keys |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Selected** | Focus ring on the display cell (`#007AFF` / `--ok-blue`). No caret. `tabIndex=0` on the active cell, `-1` on others | Arrows move **cell** (clamp, no wrap). Tab / Shift+Tab move cell (**wrap** within the lift). Enter / F2 **begin insert-edit** (no move). Printable **begin overwrite-edit**. Delete / Backspace **clear** to `null`. Ctrl/Cmd+C copies the committed display string (not `"—"` → copy `""`). Ctrl/Cmd+V overwrite-edits then commits on the usual commit keys (or commit immediately on paste — pick one and test). |
| **Editing** | The `<input>` is focused | Arrows / Home / End move **caret only**, including at string edges — **never** commit-and-move (Sheets-accurate; Excel “Enter mode” is **dropped**). Enter commits + **down same column**. Shift+Enter commits + **up same column**. Tab commits + **right with wrap**. Shift+Tab commits + **left with wrap**. Escape cancels. Delete/Backspace edit the string. |

After commit+move, the destination is **selected**, not editing.

**Click:**

- Click a different editable cell: if editing, **commit** current, **select** the target (do not auto-edit the target).
- Click already-selected: start insert-edit.
- Double-click: insert-edit.
- Click non-cell (sidebar, another control): commit if editing.

**Edges (locked):** arrows clamp (no wrap). Tab wraps within the lift and **stays** on last-set `log.rpe` / first-set `plan.kg`. Enter stays on the last row. Do **not** create sets by navigating off the bottom. Do **not** wrap Enter to `plan.kg`.

**preventDefault** on Tab / Arrows / Enter when the grid owns focus so focus does not escape to the browser chrome.

